new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8b22fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/renderer/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# smallpt WebAssembly
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), licensed under MIT (see LICENSE.txt). The original source is preserved in smallpt-original.cpp. smallpt.cpp preserves the radiance function, scene geometry, materials, camera, tent filter, and 2×2 subpixel sampling; its file-writing main is replaced by an RGBA row-rendering interface and per-sphere color setters.
+
+Build with Emscripten installed:
+
+```sh
+npm run build:wasm
+npm run build
+```
+
+The compiled JS/Wasm are checked into public/renderer, so a regular app build needs no C++ toolchain. A classic Web Worker loads the compiled module, renders small batches of rows, and transfers RGBA buffers to the page. The worker is terminated when a new render is requested. No rendering service, uploads, threads, or cross-origin isolation headers are needed.
+
+The initial preview is produced by the same C++ renderer at 800×600 and 256 spp. It is replaced by the live client-side render. The page is implemented in src/pages/index.astro and its browser controller in src/scripts/playground.ts. All asset URLs honor Astro's configured base path.
